{
  "id": "9",
  "content": "# Installable app (PWA)\n\n## What to build\n\ngraph-manager's web UI (`apps/graph-manager/src/web`, a Vite + React app served by Fastify from `dist/web`) can't be installed on a phone: it has no web app manifest, no home-screen icon (only `public/favicon.svg`) and no service worker. This slice makes it an installable app that opens full screen from the home screen on iPhone and Android:\n\n1. `public/manifest.webmanifest`, four committed PNG icons under `public/icons/` made by a new `scripts/make-icons.mjs` (agent-browser renders `favicon.svg`), and the manifest / Apple links and metas in `index.html`.\n2. `public/sw.js`: a service worker that **caches nothing**. It only answers a failed page navigation with a built-in \"graph-manager is not reachable\" page with a **Retry** button.\n3. New `src/web/ui/standalone.ts`: `isStandalone()`, `useStandaloneLinks()` (in standalone mode, same-origin `target=\"_blank\"` links open in the same window), `registerSw()` (only in a production build, on a secure context, when `serviceWorker` exists), and the captured `beforeinstallprompt` event.\n4. A new **Install app** section in Settings with four states: installed, installable (button), iOS instructions, and an HTTPS note on plain HTTP.\n5. Server (`src/server/app.ts`): `/sw.js` gets `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `/manifest.webmanifest` gets `Content-Type: application/manifest+json`; both (and the icons) load without a session.\n\nWhat earlier work already delivered (it is in the codebase; read it, don't redo it):\n- `src/web/ui/media.ts` exports `NARROW = \"(max-width: 899.98px)\"`, `PHONE = \"(max-width: 599.98px)\"`, `COARSE = \"(pointer: coarse)\"` and `useMedia(query)` (returns `false` when `window.matchMedia` is missing).\n- `src/web/index.html` already has the viewport meta `width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover, interactive-widget=resizes-content` and two `<meta name=\"theme-color\">` tags (light and dark, from the `--sf` token values); `.gm-shell` pads `env(safe-area-inset-*)`; `src/web/ui/viewport.ts` exports `useVisualViewport()`, called in `Shell.tsx`.\n- `src/web/Shell.tsx` has the phone top bar (`<header className=\"gm-topbar\" data-testid=\"gm-topbar\">` with the `nav-menu` button) and the nav drawer (`.gm-nav.drawer`, `nav-scrim`) below 900 px.\n- `src/web/pages/Settings.css` has the phone layout (e.g. `.settings-appearance-text { min-width: 0 }` below 600 px).\n- `src/server/app.ts` builds Fastify with `trustProxy: config.trustProxy` and an optional `https: { cert, key }` (`BuildAppOptions.https`), and graph-manager can serve HTTPS with `GM_TLS_CERT`/`GM_TLS_KEY`; the README has a section **HTTPS setup (phones and installing the app)** (anchor `#https-setup-phones-and-installing-the-app`) with an **Install on a phone** paragraph.\n\nOut of scope: any cache of pages or data, offline mode, push notifications, an update prompt for new versions.\n\n## Context: files to read before implementing\n\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/index.html` (whole file) — `<head>`: add the manifest and Apple tags after the `<link rel=\"icon\" ...>` line.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/main.tsx` (whole file, 23 lines) — where to register the service worker and start listening for `beforeinstallprompt`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/public/favicon.svg` (whole file) — the mark the icons are rendered from; light colours by default, dark colours under `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`: `.bg #ecedef`, `.dot #16181b`, `.edge #16181b`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/tokens.css` (lines 98–118) — dark theme: `--bg: #0e0f11`, `--sf: #16181b`, `--term: #0a0b0d`, `--termfg: #d6d9de`, `--ac: #7aa2ff`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx` (whole file; it has the top bar and drawer now) — add the two standalone hooks next to the other hooks at the top of `Shell`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Settings.tsx` (lines 173–198) — the `Settings` page; the Appearance section (:189–195) is the pattern for the new section.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Settings.css` (lines 9–12, 25–29 and the phone `@media` rules near the end) — `.settings-card`, `.settings-appearance*`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Settings.test.tsx` (lines 1–80) — `matchMedia` stub in `beforeEach`, `fakeApi()`, `renderPage()`; add the Install tests here.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.tsx` (lines 368–372) — the \"open ↗\" link (`target=\"_blank\"`, same origin `/runs/<ws>/<id>/view/`) that must open in the same window when standalone; `PrPanel.tsx:206` and `Runs.tsx:142` are GitHub links that must keep opening in the browser.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` (lines 161–170) — `fastifyStatic` registration and the SPA fallback.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.ts` (lines 52–67) — `needsAuth`: non-`/api` paths (except the run-view proxy) need no session already.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.test.ts` (lines 14–22, 60–68) — temp `webDir` with fake files; the favicon-without-cookie test to mirror.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/favicon.test.ts` (whole file) — pattern for a test that reads committed web files.\n- `apps/graph-manager/vite.config.ts` — `root: \"src/web\"`, so `src/web/public/*` is copied as-is to `dist/web/` (served at `/`).\n- `eslint.config.js` (whole file) — `public/sw.js` is a plain browser script; it needs a globals block. `apps/*/scripts/**/*.mjs` only get `process`, `console`, `URL` as globals.\n- `apps/graph-manager/package.json` (lines 10–16) — scripts; add `icons`.\n\n## Patterns to follow\n\n**Committed-file test** (`src/server/favicon.test.ts`):\n```typescript\nconst html = readFileSync(new URL(\"../web/index.html\", import.meta.url), \"utf8\");\nconst svg = readFileSync(new URL(\"../web/public/favicon.svg\", import.meta.url), \"utf8\");\nexpect(html).toContain('<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/favicon.svg\" />');\n```\n\n**Static file without a cookie** (`src/server/auth.test.ts:60-68`):\n```typescript\nconst res = await app.inject({ url: \"/favicon.svg\" });\nexpect(res.statusCode).toBe(200);\nexpect(String(res.headers[\"content-type\"])).toMatch(/^image\\/svg\\+xml/);\nexpect(needsAuth(\"GET\", \"/favicon.svg\")).toBe(false);\n```\n\n**jsdom component tests** start with `// @vitest-environment jsdom`, stub `matchMedia` with `vi.stubGlobal` (`Settings.test.tsx:9-14`), and `vi.unstubAllGlobals()` in `afterEach`. jsdom has **no** `window.isSecureContext` (it is `undefined`) and no `navigator.serviceWorker`; define them per test with `Object.defineProperty(window, \"isSecureContext\", { value: true, configurable: true })` and `Object.defineProperty(navigator, \"serviceWorker\", { value: { register: vi.fn(async () => ({})) }, configurable: true })`, and delete/redefine them in `afterEach`. User agent: `vi.spyOn(navigator, \"userAgent\", \"get\").mockReturnValue(\"Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X) ...\")`.\n\n**Settings section markup** (Appearance, `Settings.tsx:189-195`):\n```tsx\n<section className=\"settings-card settings-appearance\" aria-label=\"Appearance\" data-testid=\"appearance\">\n  <div className=\"settings-appearance-text\">\n    <h2>Appearance</h2>\n    <span className=\"field-hint\">Saved in this browser only.</span>\n  </div>\n  <Segmented ... />\n</section>\n```\n\n**agent-browser from Node** (verified on this machine; `eval` prints the result as a JSON string):\n```js\nconst ab = (...a) => execFileSync(\"agent-browser\", [\"--session\", SESSION, ...a], { encoding: \"utf8\", maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 });\nab(\"open\", \"about:blank\");\nconst out = ab(\"eval\", `(async()=>{const img=new Image();img.src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,${b64}\";await img.decode();\n  const c=document.createElement(\"canvas\");c.width=c.height=${size};const x=c.getContext(\"2d\");\n  x.fillStyle=\"#16181b\";x.fillRect(0,0,${size},${size});x.drawImage(img,${dx},${dy},${dw},${dw});return c.toDataURL(\"image/png\");})()`);\nconst dataUrl = JSON.parse(out.trim());          // \"data:image/png;base64,...\"\nwriteFileSync(file, Buffer.from(dataUrl.replace(/^data:image\\/png;base64,/, \"\"), \"base64\"));\nab(\"close\");\n```\nRendering through a canvas gives exact pixel sizes, independent of the viewport and device pixel ratio.\n\n## Step-by-step tasks\n\nExecute in order. Each task is atomic.\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/public/manifest.webmanifest`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: exactly (literal dark-theme hex values: `--bg` `#0e0f11`, `--sf` `#16181b`):\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graph-manager\",\n    \"short_name\": \"graph-manager\",\n    \"id\": \"/\",\n    \"start_url\": \"/\",\n    \"scope\": \"/\",\n    \"display\": \"standalone\",\n    \"background_color\": \"#0e0f11\",\n    \"theme_color\": \"#16181b\",\n    \"icons\": [\n      { \"src\": \"/icons/icon-192.png\", \"sizes\": \"192x192\", \"type\": \"image/png\" },\n      { \"src\": \"/icons/icon-512.png\", \"sizes\": \"512x512\", \"type\": \"image/png\" },\n      { \"src\": \"/icons/icon-maskable-512.png\", \"sizes\": \"512x512\", \"type\": \"image/png\", \"purpose\": \"maskable\" }\n    ]\n  }\n  ```\n- **GOTCHA**: re-check the two values against `src/web/ui/tokens.css` under `:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]`; if they differ, use the token values.\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/scripts/make-icons.mjs`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `node apps/graph-manager/scripts/make-icons.mjs` writes `src/web/public/icons/{apple-touch-icon.png (180), icon-192.png, icon-512.png, icon-maskable-512.png}`.\n  - Resolve paths from `fileURLToPath(new URL(\"..\", import.meta.url))` (the app folder).\n  - Read `src/web/public/favicon.svg`; replace its `<style>…</style>` block with fixed dark-scheme colours `<style>.bg{fill:#ecedef}.dot{fill:#16181b}.edge{stroke:#16181b}</style>` (headless Chrome renders the light scheme by default, and a light mark on the dark `--sf` background is what we want). Exit 1 with a message if there is no `<style>` block.\n  - For each icon: canvas filled with `#16181b` (`--sf` dark; iOS turns transparent pixels black, so icons are opaque).\n    - `apple-touch-icon.png` 180, `icon-192.png` 192, `icon-512.png` 512: draw the mark so its rounded square (x/y 1–21 of the 22 viewBox) fills the canvas: `drawImage(img, -s/20, -s/20, s*1.1, s*1.1)`.\n    - `icon-maskable-512.png` 512: the mark at 80 % size, centred: `drawImage(img, s*0.1, s*0.1, s*0.8, s*0.8)`, so Android's mask doesn't crop it.\n  - Use one agent-browser session (`--session gm-make-icons-<pid>`), `open about:blank`, one `eval` per icon (pattern above), `close` in a `finally`.\n  - Print each written file and its size.\n- **IMPORTS**: `import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\"; import { Buffer } from \"node:buffer\"; import { mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\"; import path from \"node:path\"; import { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";` (`Buffer` must be imported: eslint gives `apps/*/scripts/**/*.mjs` only `process`, `console`, `URL`).\n- **GOTCHA**: agent-browser is installed here (`agent-browser --help`). Run the script and **commit the four PNGs**; never commit placeholder images. If agent-browser fails to start, run `agent-browser install` once and retry.\n- **VALIDATE**: `node apps/graph-manager/scripts/make-icons.mjs && file apps/graph-manager/src/web/public/icons/*.png` (expect `PNG image data, 180 x 180`, `192 x 192`, `512 x 512`, `512 x 512`). Open one with the Read tool to look at it.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/package.json`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: in `scripts` add `\"icons\": \"node scripts/make-icons.mjs\"`. Not part of `build` or `test`.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/index.html`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: after `<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/favicon.svg\" />` add, in this order and this exact form (self-closing like the existing tags):\n  ```html\n  <link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.webmanifest\" />\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"/icons/apple-touch-icon.png\" />\n  <meta name=\"mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\" />\n  <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\" />\n  <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-title\" content=\"graph-manager\" />\n  <meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\" />\n  ```\n- **GOTCHA**: keep the existing viewport and theme-color metas and the inline theme script untouched; `favicon.test.ts` pins the icon link.\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/public/sw.js`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: a classic script (no imports/exports):\n  ```js\n  // graph-manager's service worker: it caches nothing. It only replaces the browser's error page when a page\n  // navigation can't reach the server (an installed app has no address bar or reload button).\n  const OFFLINE_HTML = `<!doctype html>...`;\n  self.addEventListener(\"install\", () => { self.skipWaiting(); });\n  self.addEventListener(\"activate\", (event) => { event.waitUntil(self.clients.claim()); });\n  self.addEventListener(\"fetch\", (event) => {\n    if (event.request.mode !== \"navigate\") return; // every other request goes to the network as usual\n    event.respondWith(\n      fetch(event.request).catch(\n        () => new Response(OFFLINE_HTML, { status: 503, headers: { \"content-type\": \"text/html; charset=utf-8\", \"cache-control\": \"no-store\" } }),\n      ),\n    );\n  });\n  ```\n  `OFFLINE_HTML`: `<html lang=\"en\">`, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, `<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">`, `<title>graph-manager is not reachable</title>`, inline `<style>`: `body` background `#0a0b0d` (`--term`), colour `#d6d9de` (`--termfg`), system font, centred column, `padding: max(24px, env(safe-area-inset-top)) max(24px, env(safe-area-inset-right)) max(24px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) max(24px, env(safe-area-inset-left))`; a 44 px tall button with `#7aa2ff` (`--ac`) border. Body: `<h1>graph-manager is not reachable</h1>`, `<p>Check that the server is running and that this device can reach it.</p>`, `<button type=\"button\" onclick=\"location.reload()\">Retry</button>`. No other file is loaded by the page.\n- **GOTCHA**: no `caches` API, no `respondWith` for non-navigation requests. `skipWaiting` + `clients.claim` so a new worker takes over at once.\n\n### UPDATE `eslint.config.js`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: add a block after the graph-manager web block:\n  ```js\n  // The service worker runs in the worker scope.\n  { files: [\"apps/graph-manager/src/web/public/**/*.js\"], languageOptions: { globals: { self: \"readonly\", fetch: \"readonly\", Response: \"readonly\" } } },\n  ```\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/standalone.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**:\n  ```typescript\n  /** The non-standard event Chrome, Edge and Android fire when the app can be installed. */\n  export interface BeforeInstallPromptEvent extends Event {\n    prompt(): Promise<void>;\n    userChoice: Promise<{ outcome: \"accepted\" | \"dismissed\" }>;\n  }\n\n  /** Opened from the home screen: `display-mode: standalone`, or iOS Safari's `navigator.standalone`. */\n  export function isStandalone(): boolean {\n    const mm = typeof window.matchMedia === \"function\" && window.matchMedia(\"(display-mode: standalone)\").matches;\n    return mm || (navigator as Navigator & { standalone?: boolean }).standalone === true;\n  }\n\n  /** iPhone, iPod, iPad, or an iPad that says it is a Mac (MacIntel with touch). */\n  export function isIos(nav: Pick<Navigator, \"userAgent\" | \"platform\" | \"maxTouchPoints\"> = navigator): boolean {\n    return /iPad|iPhone|iPod/.test(nav.userAgent) || (nav.platform === \"MacIntel\" && nav.maxTouchPoints > 1);\n  }\n  ```\n  - **Same-origin links in standalone**: `export function standaloneLinkHandler(e: MouseEvent): void` — if `e.defaultPrevented` or a modifier/`button !== 0`, return; find `(e.target as Element | null)?.closest?.('a[target=\"_blank\"]')`; if its `href` resolves (`new URL(a.href, location.href)`) to `location.origin`, `e.preventDefault()` and `location.assign(url.href)`. Other origins: do nothing. `export function useStandaloneLinks(): void` — `useEffect`: if `isStandalone()`, `document.addEventListener(\"click\", standaloneLinkHandler, true)` (capture) and remove it on cleanup.\n  - **Service worker**: `export function registerSw(prod: boolean = import.meta.env.PROD): boolean` — returns `false` unless `prod && window.isSecureContext === true && \"serviceWorker\" in navigator`; otherwise calls `void navigator.serviceWorker.register(\"/sw.js\").catch(() => undefined)` and returns `true`.\n  - **Install prompt**, module level so it survives until Settings mounts:\n    ```typescript\n    let deferred: BeforeInstallPromptEvent | null = null;\n    const subscribers = new Set<() => void>();\n    let listening = false;\n    /** Idempotent: keeps the first `beforeinstallprompt` (preventDefault) and forgets it on `appinstalled`. */\n    export function listenForInstallPrompt(): void { if (listening) return; listening = true;\n      window.addEventListener(\"beforeinstallprompt\", (e) => { e.preventDefault(); deferred = e as BeforeInstallPromptEvent; subscribers.forEach((f) => f()); });\n      window.addEventListener(\"appinstalled\", () => { deferred = null; subscribers.forEach((f) => f()); }); }\n    export function resetInstallPrompt(): void { deferred = null; subscribers.forEach((f) => f()); } // tests\n    ```\n    `export type InstallState = \"installed\" | \"insecure\" | \"prompt\" | \"ios\" | \"other\";`\n    `export function installState(s: { standalone: boolean; secure: boolean; hasPrompt: boolean; ios: boolean }): InstallState` — in this order: `standalone` → `\"installed\"`; `!secure` → `\"insecure\"`; `hasPrompt` → `\"prompt\"`; `ios` → `\"ios\"`; else `\"other\"`.\n    `export function useInstall(): { state: InstallState; install(): Promise<void> }` — subscribes to `subscribers` (re-render on change), computes `installState({ standalone: isStandalone(), secure: window.isSecureContext === true, hasPrompt: deferred !== null, ios: isIos() })`; `install()` calls `await deferred.prompt()`, awaits `userChoice`, then sets `deferred = null` (a prompt works once) and notifies.\n- **IMPORTS**: `import { useEffect, useState } from \"react\";`\n- **GOTCHA**: `window.matchMedia` is missing in some jsdom tests (Shell, Terminals): guard it as above. `navigator.standalone` and `BeforeInstallPromptEvent` are not in `lib.dom`; use the local types. `import.meta.env.PROD` is `false` under vitest, so tests pass `prod` explicitly.\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck -w graph-manager`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/main.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `import { listenForInstallPrompt, registerSw } from \"./ui/standalone\";` and, after `applyTheme();`: `listenForInstallPrompt();` and `registerSw();` (the condition `import.meta.env.PROD && window.isSecureContext && \"serviceWorker\" in navigator` lives in `registerSw`). Calling `listenForInstallPrompt` here, before the first render, catches the event even on the login page.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `import { listenForInstallPrompt, useStandaloneLinks } from \"./ui/standalone\";`; inside `Shell`, next to the other hooks: `useStandaloneLinks();` and `useEffect(() => listenForInstallPrompt(), []);` (idempotent; Shell captures `beforeinstallprompt` early, as the spec requires, even if `main.tsx` is not the entry, e.g. in tests).\n- **GOTCHA**: don't touch the top bar / drawer markup; `Shell.test.tsx` must keep passing.\n- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Settings.tsx` and `Settings.css`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: a new `InstallCard` rendered after the Appearance section:\n  ```tsx\n  export const HTTPS_DOCS = \"https://github.com/romm0109/graph-execution/blob/main/apps/graph-manager/README.md#https-setup-phones-and-installing-the-app\";\n  function InstallCard() {\n    const { state, install } = useInstall();\n    return (\n      <section className=\"settings-card settings-install\" aria-label=\"Install app\" data-testid=\"install-app\">\n        <div className=\"settings-install-text\">\n          <h2>Install app</h2>\n          {state === \"installed\" && <span className=\"field-hint\" data-testid=\"install-installed\">Installed.</span>}\n          {state === \"insecure\" && (\n            <span className=\"field-hint\" data-testid=\"install-https\">\n              Installing needs HTTPS. See <a href={HTTPS_DOCS} target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">HTTPS setup in the README</a>.\n            </span>\n          )}\n          {state === \"ios\" && <span className=\"field-hint\" data-testid=\"install-ios\">In Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen.</span>}\n          {state === \"other\" && <span className=\"field-hint\" data-testid=\"install-other\">Open graph-manager on your phone to install it from the browser.</span>}\n        </div>\n        {state === \"prompt\" && (\n          <button type=\"button\" className=\"btn btn-primary\" data-testid=\"install-button\" onClick={() => void install()}>\n            Install app\n          </button>\n        )}\n      </section>\n    );\n  }\n  ```\n  The visible HTTPS text must read \"Installing needs HTTPS. See HTTPS setup in the README.\" (the link text is \"HTTPS setup in the README\").\n  `Settings.css`: `.settings-install` and `.settings-install-text` copy `.settings-appearance` / `.settings-appearance-text` (lines 25–26); add `.settings-install-text` to the phone rule that sets `.settings-appearance-text { min-width: 0 }`.\n- **IMPORTS**: `import { useInstall } from \"../ui/standalone\";`\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck -w graph-manager`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: the `fastifyStatic` registration (line 163) gets `setHeaders`:\n  ```typescript\n  await app.register(fastifyStatic, {\n    root: webDir, wildcard: false, index: false,\n    // The service worker must be re-checked on every load; the manifest's type is not in every mime table.\n    setHeaders: (reply, filePath) => {\n      if (path.basename(filePath) === \"sw.js\") reply.header(\"cache-control\", \"no-cache\");\n      if (filePath.endsWith(\".webmanifest\")) reply.header(\"content-type\", \"application/manifest+json\");\n    },\n  });\n  ```\n- **GOTCHA**: `setHeaders` receives the Fastify `reply` in `@fastify/static` 10 (`types/index.d.ts:97`) and runs after the default `cache-control: public, max-age=0`, so it overrides it. No auth change: `needsAuth` already returns `false` for `/sw.js`, `/manifest.webmanifest` and `/icons/*`.\n- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck -w graph-manager`\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/pwa.test.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT** (node environment):\n  - Committed files: `manifest.webmanifest` parses as JSON and equals the object above (`display: \"standalone\"`, the three icons, `background_color: \"#0e0f11\"`, `theme_color: \"#16181b\"`); each icon file exists and its PNG size is right — read `buf.readUInt32BE(16)` (width) and `buf.readUInt32BE(20)` (height) after checking the 8-byte PNG signature: `apple-touch-icon.png` 180, `icon-192.png` 192, `icon-512.png` 512, `icon-maskable-512.png` 512; `index.html` contains the six tags above.\n  - Server: a temp `webDir` (as `auth.test.ts:14-22`) with `index.html`, `app.js`, `sw.js` (`self.addEventListener(\"fetch\", () => {})`), `manifest.webmanifest` (`{}`) and `icons/icon-192.png` (copy any committed icon); `buildApp(testConfig(dir), { webDir, viewCache: false })`. Without a cookie: `GET /manifest.webmanifest` → 200, `content-type` matches `/^application\\/manifest\\+json/`; `GET /sw.js` → 200 and `cache-control` is `no-cache`; `GET /icons/icon-192.png` → 200 `image/png`; `needsAuth(\"GET\", \"/sw.js\")` and `needsAuth(\"GET\", \"/manifest.webmanifest\")` are `false`; other files keep their old headers (`GET /app.js` still has `cache-control: public, max-age=0`).\n- **PATTERN**: `src/server/favicon.test.ts`, `src/server/auth.test.ts:60-68`.\n- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/server/pwa.test.ts`\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/sw.test.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT** (node environment): load `public/sw.js` with a fake worker scope:\n  ```typescript\n  const src = readFileSync(new URL(\"./public/sw.js\", import.meta.url), \"utf8\");\n  function load(fetchImpl: (r: unknown) => Promise<Response>) {\n    const listeners: Record<string, (e: any) => void> = {};\n    const self = { addEventListener: (t: string, f: (e: any) => void) => (listeners[t] = f), skipWaiting: vi.fn(), clients: { claim: vi.fn(async () => {}) } };\n    new Function(\"self\", \"fetch\", \"Response\", src)(self, fetchImpl, Response);\n    return { listeners, self };\n  }\n  ```\n  Tests: `install` calls `skipWaiting`; `activate` calls `waitUntil` with `clients.claim()`; a navigation (`{ request: { mode: \"navigate\" }, respondWith: vi.fn() }`) whose `fetch` rejects (`new TypeError(\"Failed to fetch\")`) → `respondWith` got a promise of a `Response` with status 503, `content-type` `text/html`, and text containing `graph-manager is not reachable`, `Check that the server is running and that this device can reach it.`, `Retry` and `location.reload()`; a navigation whose fetch resolves passes that response through; a request with `mode: \"cors\"` or `\"no-cors\"` → `respondWith` not called and `fetch` not called. Also assert `src` does not contain `caches.`.\n- **GOTCHA**: use `unknown`/narrow types instead of `any` if lint complains (`@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` is on in `recommended`).\n- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/sw.test.ts`\n\n### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/standalone.test.ts`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT** (`// @vitest-environment jsdom`):\n  - `isStandalone`: `matchMedia` stub with `matches: true` → true; `matches: false` and `navigator.standalone` undefined → false; `Object.defineProperty(navigator, \"standalone\", { value: true, configurable: true })` → true; no `matchMedia` at all → false (no throw).\n  - `isIos`: iPhone UA → true; `{ userAgent: \"Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh...)\", platform: \"MacIntel\", maxTouchPoints: 5 }` → true; same with `maxTouchPoints: 0` → false; an Android UA → false.\n  - Links: render a hook host (`renderHook(() => useStandaloneLinks())` from `@testing-library/react`) with standalone stubbed true; replace `location.assign` via `vi.spyOn(window.location, \"assign\")` if configurable, else `vi.stubGlobal(\"location\", { ...})` — simplest: test `standaloneLinkHandler` directly with a real `<a href=\"/runs/ws/r/view/\" target=\"_blank\">` appended to `document.body` and a `MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, button: 0 })` dispatched on it, with `location.assign` spied → called with `http://localhost:3000/runs/ws/r/view/` and the event `defaultPrevented`; an `<a href=\"https://github.com/o/r/pull/1\" target=\"_blank\">` → not prevented, `assign` not called; an `<a>` without `target` → not touched. With standalone false, `useStandaloneLinks` adds no listener (a click on the same-origin link is not prevented).\n  - `registerSw`: with `navigator.serviceWorker = { register: vi.fn(async () => ({})) }` and `isSecureContext` true: `registerSw(true)` → true and `register(\"/sw.js\")`; `registerSw(false)` → false; `isSecureContext` false → false; no `serviceWorker` in navigator → false. Never called in any false case.\n  - `installState` table for all five outcomes, including the order (`standalone` beats everything, `!secure` beats `hasPrompt`).\n- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/ui/standalone.test.ts`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Settings.test.tsx`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: a `describe(\"Install app\")` block (call `resetInstallPrompt()` and remove `isSecureContext` in `afterEach`):\n  - `isSecureContext` false (or undefined, jsdom's default) → `install-https` shows \"Installing needs HTTPS. See HTTPS setup in the README.\" and its link `href` equals `HTTPS_DOCS`.\n  - `isSecureContext` true and an iPhone user agent → `install-ios` with \"In Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen.\"\n  - `isSecureContext` true, desktop UA, then `listenForInstallPrompt()` and `act(() => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(\"beforeinstallprompt\", { cancelable: true }), { prompt: vi.fn(async () => {}), userChoice: Promise.resolve({ outcome: \"accepted\" }) })))` → `install-button` appears; clicking it calls `prompt` once and the button goes away.\n  - `matchMedia` stubbed so `(display-mode: standalone)` matches → `install-installed` \"Installed.\".\n- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Settings.test.tsx`\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/README.md`\n\n- **IMPLEMENT**: in the **Install on a phone** paragraph (under HTTPS setup) add one sentence: the app has a small service worker that caches nothing; when the server can't be reached the installed app shows \"graph-manager is not reachable\" with **Retry**; Settings → **Install app** shows the install button (Chrome, Edge, Android), the iPhone steps, or why it can't be installed on plain HTTP. Mention `npm run icons -w graph-manager` regenerates the icons from `favicon.svg` (needs agent-browser) in the Local development section.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `GET /manifest.webmanifest` (no cookie) is 200 with `content-type: application/manifest+json` and returns the manifest with `display: \"standalone\"` and the 192, 512 and maskable 512 icons.\n- [ ] `GET /sw.js` (no cookie) is 200 with `cache-control: no-cache`. `/icons/*.png` load without a cookie.\n- [ ] `index.html` links the manifest and `/icons/apple-touch-icon.png` and has the `mobile-web-app-capable`, `apple-mobile-web-app-capable`, `apple-mobile-web-app-title` and `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style=black-translucent` metas.\n- [ ] The four PNGs are committed at 180, 192, 512 and 512 px, opaque, made by `scripts/make-icons.mjs` from `favicon.svg`; the maskable one has the mark at 80 %.\n- [ ] `sw.js` caches nothing, handles only navigations, and answers a failed one with \"graph-manager is not reachable\", \"Check that the server is running and that this device can reach it.\" and a **Retry** button (`location.reload()`), dark `--term` colours, safe-area padding.\n- [ ] The service worker is registered only when `import.meta.env.PROD`, `window.isSecureContext` and `\"serviceWorker\" in navigator` are all true (not in the Vite dev server, not on plain HTTP).\n- [ ] In standalone mode, a same-origin `target=\"_blank\"` link (run page \"open ↗\") opens in the same window; a GitHub PR link still opens in the browser.\n- [ ] Settings → Install app shows: \"Installed.\" when standalone; the **Install app** button after a captured `beforeinstallprompt` (it calls `prompt()`); \"In Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen.\" on iOS; \"Installing needs HTTPS. See HTTPS setup in the README.\" with a link on plain HTTP.\n- [ ] `beforeinstallprompt` is captured before Settings mounts (in `main.tsx` and Shell).\n- [ ] Desktop behaviour is unchanged; `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` pass.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n```bash\n# Type / lint\nnpm run typecheck && npm run lint\n\n# Tests for this slice\ncd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/server/pwa.test.ts src/server/favicon.test.ts src/web/sw.test.ts src/web/ui/standalone.test.ts src/web/Settings.test.tsx src/web/Shell.test.tsx && cd ../..\n\n# Build: the public files land in dist/web\nnpm run build -w graph-manager && ls apps/graph-manager/dist/web/manifest.webmanifest apps/graph-manager/dist/web/sw.js apps/graph-manager/dist/web/icons/\n\n# Whole suite\nnpm test\n```\n\nManual check with agent-browser (as `apps/graph-manager/scripts/ui-smoke.sh` does): start the built server with `GM_PASSWORD=pw GM_PORT=7499 node apps/graph-manager/dist/server/main.js`, `agent-browser open http://127.0.0.1:7499/settings` (localhost is a secure context), log in, check the Install app section and `agent-browser eval \"navigator.serviceWorker.getRegistration().then(r => !!r)\"` → `true`.\n\nKnown environment failure: `packages/graph-execution/src/cli.test.ts` \"exits 2 at startup when --provider claude is not on the PATH\" fails wherever a real `claude` is installed next to `node`; ignore it.\n",
